\DOC LOCAL_NSQR_SAFETY_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_NSQR_SAFETY_TAC : string -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Discharges a subroutine call inside an {eventually} goal by applying a named
{ensures} specification assumption, replacing the pre-call state in the
conclusion by a fresh post-call state and rewriting the assumptions to describe
that new state.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument {assump_name : string} is the label of the assumed {ensures}
specification, held in the goal's assumption list, to be used for the call; the
second argument {n : int} is the index from which the name of the new post-call
state variable is formed (the successor of the pre-call state's index). The
goal's conclusion is {eventually ... s_n}, with assumptions {A} describing
state {s_n}: program bytes loaded, register and memory reads, event trace, and
an accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation from the initial state. The tactic yields
exactly one subgoal, whose conclusion is the same {eventually ...} applied to a
fresh state {s_{n+1}}:
{
   A ?- eventually ... s_n
   ================================  LOCAL_NSQR_SAFETY_TAC assump_name n
   A' ?- eventually ... s_{n+1}
}
\noindent Here {A'} is obtained as follows. The assumptions describing the
pre-call state — program counter, argument registers, flag values, event trace,
saved register/memory reads, {MAYCHANGE} — are removed and replaced by
corresponding assumptions about the new state: the program counter at the
callee's return address, an event trace equation prefixing a freshly named
existential event list to the previous trace, two new assumptions
characterising that event list via the callee's event function and a
{memaccess_inbounds} property, the preserved register and memory reads restated
at the new state, and an extended {MAYCHANGE} relation. The specification
assumption named by {assump_name} is consumed from its position and re-added at
the end of the assumption list, as is the other specification assumption
present; the {nonoverlapping} side conditions and previously accumulated
event/{memaccess_inbounds} facts are retained.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single-subgoal transformation on goals that
already carry such a specification assumption.

\ENDDOC
